  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support towards Pope Francis&apos; Visit to Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to ensure the proper planning and execution of the Holy Father&apos;s itinerary in Kenya with the mandate to plan and coordinate various activities to ensure a successful visit of the Pope.
In November 2015, Pope Francis will make his maiden visit to Africa in a tour that will see him in three countries that have suffered Christian persecution and religious extremism. He will hold a meeting with religious groups, including mainstream Christian evangelicals, Muslims and Hindus to discuss challenges of religious tolerance and strategies towards a co -existence for a stable nation. 
To ensure proper planning and execution of the Holy Father&apos;s itinerary in Kenya, KCCB has formed a Papal Secretariat with the mandate to plan and coordinate various activities to ensure successful visit of the Pope. The Caritas Forum (CCF) partners meeting made an urgent financial appeal to CI member organisations (CIMOs) in Kenya for support to facilitate the Holy Father&apos;s visit.</narrative>
  </description>
